cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on the architectural innovations described here, please cite it as below."
title: "Φ-Plasma-Core: Symplectic-Hamiltonian Token Flow with Hecke-Eigensheaf Attention"
abstract: >-
  A novel transformer-style language model architecture combining
  symplectic Hamiltonian flow over (q, p) phase-space tokens with
  Hecke-algebra structured head mixing, trained with a Störmer-Verlet
  symplectic optimizer. Demonstrates 2.31× more stable validation
  perplexity across context length doublings (1K to 64K) than a
  parameter-matched vanilla transformer baseline at the same training
  budget, on WikiText-2 with 15M-42M parameter models.
authors:
